    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when at least one of two types derives from <computeroutput>op</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the left-hand operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the right-hand operand.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>any_op</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>Lhs_T</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>Rhs_T</computeroutput> (or both) are derived from the <computeroutput>type_traits::op</computeroutput> base struct. It is used to constrain binary operator overloads in the <computeroutput>operators</computeroutput> namespace so that they are enabled only when at least one operand is a framework type, avoiding unintended conflicts with user-defined operators. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
